direction: down
title: "STATE DOMAIN AND PRESERVATION BOUNDARY\nK = CANCELED | UNWIND; I belongs to legacy trace state"
title.shape: text
source: "Pinned whole-word behavior\nsaved = flags; callback may mutate K\nrestore flags = saved"
effect: "Old cancellation projection becomes saved K\nNew cancellation may be erased\nConsumed state may be restored"
qualify: "Reachability is separate\nReadiness can consume C or reject U before body\nBit algebra is not a native scenario result"
split: "Proposed one authoritative CancelCell\nTraceFrame saves only legacy projection excluding K\nAll checks / resets / private writers must migrate"
restore: "Restore at the same source point\nLegacy projection = saved legacy projection\nCancelCell receives NO trace-exit mutation"
preserve: "Preservation target\nOriginal recursion scopes, list order, code/result fold\nOriginal non-cancellation projection at restore"
change: "Explicit semantic change\nOld trace erasure / replay histories differ\nNo writable shadow; no full equivalence claim\nDELETED and other legacy lifecycle effects still qualify"
source -> effect -> qualify -> split -> restore
restore -> preserve
restore -> change
qualify.style.fill: "#FFF0E5"
split.style.fill: "#DFEEFF"
change.style.fill: "#FFF0E5"
preserve.style.fill: "#E8F4E8"
